 API produced by the report computation work; consumer follows producer. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same — the export/semantics docs must also cover the admin view. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|-------------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002, RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Split across the component boundary (Rule 1): computation and API in the Distributed Workloads epic, administrator-facing view in the Dashboard epic. Both are P0. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: CSV export and the stable API are retrieval modes of the same report data structure and API surface the P0 computation produces; a split would double-touch the same code and build the same API endpoint twice. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: the quota comparison renders inside the same admin view / UI surface as the P0 consumption report; a split would build the same view twice with an artificial serialization edge. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Separate `docs-authoring` epic: substantive new doc topics are a distinct work-product type. Priority P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1). |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Team