{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bcd5d030-5f3b-4f9f-8fe5-f7640329ec24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1d788cd87cdb833","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-g7ffw5dm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n\n## Description\n\nResolves the strategy's open question — the per-project GPU-hour metering data\nschema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990)\nand is not final until that strategy lands — by producing a pinned consumption\ncontract that the chargeback reporting work builds against. The deliverable is\na written contract plus a stability assessment and a consumption-approach\ndecision; it does not re-implement or alter the metering collection pipeline\nitself (explicitly out of scope).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate the metering data schema as currently designed by the in-flight\n  metering strategy: fields, the per-project attribution key, time granularity,\n  and data availability/retention.\n- Assess the stability of each element (final vs. in flux) and identify the\n  subset that chargeback reporting can safely build against.\n- Decide the consumption approach: consume the schema directly, or isolate the\n  reporting work behind an adaptation layer so schema drift does not cascade\n  into the reporting surfaces.\n- Map each reporting surface's data needs (per-project GPU-hour reports,\n  selectable time ranges, current-month consumption, CSV/API export) to\n  contract elements; raise unmapped needs with the metering strategy owners.\n- Publish the consumption contract and record alignment (or open items with\n  owners) with the metering strategy team.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written consumption contract exists covering fields, per-project\n  attribution, time granularity, and availability, with each element marked\n  final or in-flux.\n- A consume-directly vs. isolation-layer recommendation is recorded, with the\n  criteria that motivated it.\n- Every reporting surface's data needs are mapped to contract elements; any\n  unmapped need is documented and raised with the metering strategy owners.\n- Alignment with the metering strategy owners is recorded — either sign-off\n  on the contract or a list of open items with owners and a resolution path.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Does not directly deliver an HLR; it gates HLR-1 (P0), HLR-2 (P1), and\n  HLR-3 (P1) by determining how all reporting surfaces consume the metering\n  data those HLRs compute from.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The metering schema is not final until the metering strategy lands; the\n  contract may need revision, and downstream reporting implementations carry\n  a rewrite gate (recorded in their frontmatter `gate_failure_impact`) with an\n  isolation-layer fallback.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47027,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b578be8699c1736d","agent_id":"aa596b517219ccaf0","session_id":"17116bf2-6a20-4da5-9984-1c3653ad446c","uuid":"6a72765a-ea84-41c7-886f-155330fe7bc8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:27:50.522Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
