{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bcd5d030-5f3b-4f9f-8fe5-f7640329ec24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea1545a208c1f41","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-g7ffw5dm/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour report computation and reporting API\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the backend capability that computes per-project GPU-hour consumption\nreports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the\nGPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), and exposes those reports\nthrough a stable API with CSV export for finance tooling. Reports are in\nGPU-hours; currency/cost-rate modelling is out of scope. This epic consumes\nthe metering data — it must not re-implement collection.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Report computation: per-project GPU-hour totals over selectable time ranges,\n  conforming to the pinned metering data consumption contract and its\n  GPU-hour semantics.\n- CSV export of the computed reports.\n- A stable, versioned reporting API that finance tooling can retrieve reports\n  from.\n- Validation of computed reports against metering data as actually delivered,\n  where available, triaging any deviation from the pinned contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metering data conforming to the pinned consumption contract,\n  per-project GPU-hour totals are computed correctly over selectable time\n  ranges, per the contract's GPU-hour semantics.\n- Reports are exportable as CSV with well-defined headers, one row per\n  project, and the selected time-range bounds stated.\n- The reporting API is versioned and documented; a finance-tooling consumer\n  can retrieve a per-project report for a chosen time range.\n- Where metering data from the in-flight metering strategy is available,\n  computed reports are validated against it, and any deviation from the pinned\n  contract is triaged and documented.\n- Existing build/CI pipelines for the touched repositories remain green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — the report computation portion of the administrator-facing\n  consumption reports.\n- HLR-2 (P1) — CSV export and the stable API for finance tooling; these are\n  retrieval modes of the same report data structure, so they are delivered\n  with the P0 computation rather than as a separate epic.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when the\n  in-flight metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands. Mitigation: build\n  against the pinned consumption contract, with an isolation/adaptation layer\n  if the contract's stability assessment recommends one. This schedule risk is\n  outside this epic's control and is tracked at the strategy level.\n- Component placement note: this work is assigned to the Distributed Workloads\n  component because the Dashboard owns no data plane per its architecture\n  context — time-range aggregation and a reporting service are backend\n  functions.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47027,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b578be8699c1736d","agent_id":"aa596b517219ccaf0","session_id":"17116bf2-6a20-4da5-9984-1c3653ad446c","uuid":"7474c21e-c949-48ef-be85-03e790d77af4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:27:58.654Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
