{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8c7a056cf914ab","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's open question — the per-project GPU-hour metering data\n30\tschema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990)\n31\tand is not final until that strategy lands — by producing a pinned consumption\n32\tcontract that the chargeback reporting work builds against. The deliverable is\n33\ta written contract plus a stability assessment and a consumption-approach\n34\tdecision; it does not re-implement or alter the metering collection pipeline\n35\titself (explicitly out of scope).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Enumerate the metering data schema as currently designed by the in-flight\n40\t  metering strategy: fields, the per-project attribution key, time granularity,\n41\t  and data availability/retention.\n42\t- Assess the stability of each element (final vs. in flux) and identify the\n43\t  subset that chargeback reporting can safely build against.\n44\t- Decide the consumption approach: consume the schema directly, or isolate the\n45\t  reporting work behind an adaptation layer so schema drift does not cascade\n46\t  into the reporting surfaces.\n47\t- Map each reporting surface's data needs (per-project GPU-hour reports,\n48\t  selectable time ranges, current-month consumption, CSV/API export) to\n49\t  contract elements; raise unmapped needs with the metering strategy owners.\n50\t- Publish the consumption contract and record alignment (or open items with\n51\t  owners) with the metering strategy team.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A written consumption contract exists covering fields, per-project\n56\t  attribution, time granularity, and availability, with each element marked\n57\t  final or in-flux.\n58\t- A consume-directly vs. isolation-layer recommendation is recorded, with the\n59\t  criteria that motivated it.\n60\t- Every reporting surface's data needs are mapped to contract elements; any\n61\t  unmapped need is documented and raised with the metering strategy owners.\n62\t- Alignment with the metering strategy owners is recorded — either sign-off\n63\t  on the contract or a list of open items with owners and a resolution path.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- Does not directly deliver an HLR; it gates HLR-1 (P0), HLR-2 (P1), and\n68\t  HLR-3 (P1) by determining how all reporting surfaces consume the metering\n69\t  data those HLRs compute from.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- The metering schema is not final until the metering strategy lands; the\n74\t  contract may need revision, and downstream reporting implementations carry\n75\t  a rewrite gate (recorded in their frontmatter `gate_failure_impact`) with an\n76\t  isolation-layer fallback.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e56fc9759bbf85d","agent_id":"add6bbde06547dd45","session_id":"17116bf2-6a20-4da5-9984-1c3653ad446c","uuid":"145c277b-eba6-4982-b6a5-583b028fd6f3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:29:56.836Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8c7a056cf914ab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_typ