{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8512266c063b6047","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour report computation and reporting API\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If no stable subset of the metering data schema can be pinned,\n15\t    re-scope the report computation to consume through an isolation/adaptation layer\n16\t    and defer final schema wiring until the GPU usage metering strategy lands.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 0\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 0\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Per-project GPU-hour report computation and reporting API\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDelivers the backend capability that computes per-project GPU-hour consumption\n39\treports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the\n40\tGPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), and exposes those reports\n41\tthrough a stable API with CSV export for finance tooling. Reports are in\n42\tGPU-hours; currency/cost-rate modelling is out of scope. This epic consumes\n43\tthe metering data — it must not re-implement collection.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Report computation: per-project GPU-hour totals over selectable time ranges,\n48\t  conforming to the pinned metering data consumption contract and its\n49\t  GPU-hour semantics.\n50\t- CSV export of the computed reports.\n51\t- A stable, versioned reporting API that finance tooling can retrieve reports\n52\t  from.\n53\t- Validation of computed reports against metering data as actually delivered,\n54\t  where available, triaging any deviation from the pinned contract.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given metering data conforming to the pinned consumption contract,\n59\t  per-project GPU-hour totals are computed correctly over selectable time\n60\t  ranges, per the contract's GPU-hour semantics.\n61\t- Reports are exportable as CSV with well-defined headers, one row per\n62\t  project, and the selected time-range bounds stated.\n63\t- The reporting API is versioned and documented; a finance-tooling consumer\n64\t  can retrieve a per-project report for a chosen time range.\n65\t- Where metering data from the in-flight metering strategy is available,\n66\t  computed reports are validated against it, and any deviation from the pinned\n67\t  contract is triaged and documented.\n68\t- Existing build/CI pipelines for the touched repositories remain green.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P0) — the report computation portion of the administrator-facing\n73\t  consumption reports.\n74\t- HLR-2 (P1) — CSV export and the stable API for finance tooling; these are\n75\t  retrieval modes of the same report data structure, so they are delivered\n76\t  with the P0 computation rather than as a separate epic.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- External timing risk: the metering data schema finalizes only when the\n81\t  in-flight metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands. Mitigation: build\n82\t  against the pinned consumption contract, with an isolation/adaptation layer\n83\t  if the contract's stability assessment recommends one. This schedule risk is\n84\t  outside this epic's control and is tracked at the strategy level.\n85\t- Component placement note: this work is assigned to the Distributed Workloads\n86\t  component because the Dashboard owns no data plane per its architecture\n87\t  context — time-range aggregation and a reporting service are backend\n88\t  functions.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e56fc9759bbf85d","agent_id":"add6bbde06547dd45","session_id":"17116bf2-6a20-4da5-9984-1c3653ad446c","uuid":"bbcd5270-c778-4bd3-804c-7dfe65d5d781","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:29:57.454Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8512266c063b6047","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
