{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a160a3a621d4378f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9018 (GPU chargeback reporting for platform administrators)\n10\t\n11\tTriage (Step 0): full decomposition. The strategy is not below-threshold — it\n12\tspans two components (Dashboard, Distributed Workloads) and two owning teams,\n13\tand its scope spans architecturally distinct work streams (backend report\n14\tcomputation and reporting API, frontend Dashboard admin view, documentation\n15\tauthoring). It contains a flagged open question (metering data schema), a\n16\tgenuine unknown that gates downstream work. It is not documentation-only.\n17\t\n18\tStrategy sections noted as missing (health warning, decomposition proceeded\n19\twith available information): Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n20\tAcceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), Non-Functional Requirements, Staff\n21\tEngineer Input. Owning teams were inferred from the architecture context files\n22\t(see Health Warnings).\n23\t\n24\t## Epic List\n25\t\n26\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n27\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Metering data consumption contract for GPU chargeback reporting | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Per-project GPU-hour report computation and reporting API | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Dashboard admin view for GPU chargeback reporting | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | GPU chargeback reporting documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n32\t\n33\t## Component Mapping Notes\n34\t\n35\t- **Reporting backend → Distributed Workloads (canonical component).** The\n36\t  strategy lists Distributed Workloads as affected but gives no change\n37\t  description. The report computation and reporting API are placed here\n38\t  because the Dashboard architecture context (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`)\n39\t  states the Dashboard \"owns no data plane\" and its interfaces are\n40\t  \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\" — a time-range aggregation\n41\t  and reporting service cannot live in the Dashboard. Distributed Workloads\n42\t  owns the GPU workload/quota domain the reports are computed over.\n43\t- **Admin view → Dashboard.** Direct mapping; the Dashboard is the platform's\n44\t  administrator-facing console.\n45\t- **Documentation → Documentation.** Added for HLR-4; the strategy's Affected\n46\t  Components list names only Dashboard and Distributed Workloads, but HLR-4 is\n47\t  a substantive docs-authoring work stream (new doc topics, not incidental\n48\t  touch-ups), which warrants a separate `docs-authoring` epic per the\n49\t  work-product-type boundary rule.\n50\t- All component values are copied verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n51\t\n52\t## Dependency DAG\n53\t\n54\t```mermaid\n55\tgraph TD\n56\t    E001[\"E001 Metering data consumption contract (Investigation)\"]\n57\t    E002[\"E002 Report computation and reporting API\"]\n58\t    E003[\"E003 Dashboard admin chargeback view\"]\n59\t    E004[\"E004 Chargeback reporting documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n60\t    E001 --> E002\n61\t    E002 --> E003\n62\t    E002 --> E004\n63\t    E003 --> E004\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t## DAG Justification\n67\t\n68\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n69\t|------|------|-----------|\n70\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | The metering data consumption contract determines how the report computation consumes metering data — a `rewrite` gate. If no stable subset can be pinned, the computation is re-scoped behind an isolation/adaptation layer. The epics exist either way, so no conditional branch epics; the gate is recorded as `gate_failure_impact` on E002. |\n71\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard admin view builds against the reporting API produced by the report computation work; consumer follows producer. |\n72\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n73\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same — the export/semantics docs must also cover the admin view. |\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n76\t\n77\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) | Notes |\n78\t|-----|----------|-------------|---------|-------|\n79\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002, RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Split across the component boundary (Rule 1): computation and API in the Distributed Workloads epic, administrator-facing view in the Dashboard epic. Both are P0. |\n80\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: CSV export and the stable API are retrieval modes of the same report data structure and API surface the P0 computation produces; a split would double-touch the same code and build the same API endpoint twice. |\n81\t| HLR-3 | P1 | The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: the quota comparison renders inside the same admin view / UI surface as the P0 consumption report; a split would build the same view twice with an artificial serialization edge. |\n82\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration. | RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Separate `docs-authoring` epic: substantive new doc topics are a distinct work-product type. Priority P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1). |\n83\t\n84\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n85\t\n86\t## Health Warnings\n87\t\n88\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n89\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n90\t  non-functional requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were therefore derived\n91\t  from the HLRs. Owning teams were inferred from the architecture context\n92\t  (`RHOAI Dashboard` and `Distributed Workloads` per\n93\t  `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`); the documentation\n94\t  epic's team (`RHOAI Documentation`) is inferred — verify with the docs owner.\n95\t- **External timing risk (open question 1)**: the metering data schema\n96\t  finalizes only when the in-flight metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) lands.\n97\t  This is a schedule risk carried by the report computation work, not an\n98\t  acceptance criterion (it is not controlled by this strategy). Mitigation:\n99\t  the consumption-contract Investigation gates the report computation, with an\n100\t  isolation-layer fallback recorded in `gate_failure_impact`, and the report\n101\t  computation's acceptance criteria validate output against the pinned\n102\t  contract and, where available, delivered metering data.\n103\t- **Dashboard data-access surface**: `architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`\n104\t  states the Dashboard's interfaces are \"Kubernetes API only; no private\n105\t  component APIs\" and that it owns no data plane. The exact surface through\n106\t  which the admin view consumes report data must respect that constraint —\n107\t  this is an implementation decision for the Dashboard and reporting teams\n108\t  (not designed here), and it reinforced the placement of the report\n109\t  computation in the Distributed Workloads component.\n110\t\n111\t## Tiered Delivery\n112\t\n113\tExternal dependency with uncertain timing: the per-project GPU-hour metering\n114\tdata delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990 (in flight, separate strategy; frontmatter\n115\t`depends-on` link). Evaluation per Rule 18 / Step 5.5:\n116\t\n117\t1. Can the strategy deliver partial value without it? **Only risk-reduction\n118\t   value.** Every user-facing HLR (reports, admin view, export) computes from\n119\t   metering data; the Kueue-quota side of the admin view is available today\n120\t   but renders in the same UI surface as the consumption view, so it does not\n121\t   warrant a separate Tier 1 feature epic.\n122\t2. Split applied:\n123\t   - **Tier 1 (independent work)**: the consumption-contract Investigation —\n124\t     a risk-reduction validation that starts immediately and does not need the\n125\t     metering strategy to land.\n126\t   - **Tier 2 (dependency-gated work)**: the report computation and the\n127\t     Dashboard admin view proceed against the pinned consumption contract;\n128\t     final validation against the landed metering data is an acceptance\n129\t     criterion on the report computation, and the rewrite-gate fallback\n130\t     (isolation layer) covers schema drift.\n131\t3. RHAISTRAT-9990 is an internal in-flight strategy, not a third party or\n132\t   upstream community dependency, so it is modeled as a precondition with\n133\t   tiered delivery — no external-dependency Implementation epic and no\n134\t   upstream PR/RFC epic.\n135\t\n136\tNo konflux-onboarding, license-validation, or repo-onboarding epics are\n137\tneeded: both Dashboard and Distributed Workloads are already Konflux-onboarded\n138\tper their architecture context files, and no new component is introduced.\n139\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9723d0ab7cfb4774","agent_id":"af544191e222ad3e5","session_id":"17116bf2-6a20-4da5-9984-1c3653ad446c","uuid":"02a73306-cd9f-441a-91a0-f7e77a69e448","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:34:04.491Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a160a3a621d4378f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"confi